# SES after-action email encoding (agent rule)

Canonical helper: `scripts/send_after_action_email.py`

## Problem (recurring)

Production after-action emails arrived in Gmail with literal `\n` and `\u2014` instead of
line breaks and em dashes (v0.5.67, v0.5.68, v0.5.70, v0.5.71). Recipients saw escaped
garbage, not HTML.

## Root cause

Agents ran `json.dumps(html)` (or equivalent) and then passed the result into AWS CLI
shorthand:

```bash
# BROKEN — double-escapes newlines/Unicode into the SES Data field
aws ses send-email --message "Body={Html={Data=$(python3 -c 'import json; print(json.dumps(html))'),Charset=utf-8}}"
```

SES then delivered those escape sequences as plain characters.

## Required fix

1. Write **real UTF-8 HTML** to a file (heredoc with real newlines is fine).
2. Send only via:

```bash
python3 scripts/send_after_action_email.py \
  --subject "YourApp Production After-Action — vX.Y.Z (ALL SYSTEMS GREEN)" \
  --html-file /tmp/after-action.html
```

The helper builds the SES JSON payload **once** with `json.dump` and calls
`aws ses send-email --cli-input-json file://… --profile yourapp --region ap-southeast-2`.

## Forbidden

- `json.dumps(html)` into `--message "Body={Html={Data=…}}"`
- Any shell packing of HTML into the SES shorthand `--message` string
- Skipping the helper “just this once”

